# Template drift allowlist for zudo-css-wisdom.
# Generated projects start from create-zudo-doc templates; this file records
# intentional host customizations that `pnpm check:template-drift` preserves.
#
# Format: one repo-relative path per line (no leading slash).
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# Reconciled against the create-zudo-doc 5.22.0 baseline on 2026-09-12 and
# re-verified against 5.27.0 on 2026-09-25: every tracked template file except
# scripts/check-links.js is byte-identical between 5.22.0 and 5.27.0, so the
# "5.22.0" references below still describe the current template. check-links.js
# was re-adopted verbatim from 5.27.0 and remains drift-gated.
# All ten base files plus the i18n doc-route file were compared individually.
# The eight entries below retain host behavior or branding; no entry exists
# merely to make the check green. pages/index.tsx, scripts/check-links.js,
# and src/styles/global.css match the templates and are actively drift-gated.
# Other feature file sets (tauri / tauriDev) were not scaffolded for this site.

# ── DocHistory-patched route stubs ────────────────────────────────────────
# The 5.22.0 base and i18n stubs receive a DocHistory patch when create-zudo-doc
# scaffolds the docHistory feature. `docHistory: true` remains enabled here.
# Keep the imports from "@takazudo/zudo-doc/doc-history" and
# "@takazudo/zudo-doc/chrome-bindings", plus the defineChromeBindings spread
# over chromeBindings, so the history button hydrates on both dynamic routes.
# The updated 5.22.0 route comments are adopted. These imports and the binding
# merge are the ONLY remaining differences from the unpatched templates.
pages/docs/[[...slug]].tsx
pages/[locale]/docs/[[...slug]].tsx

# ── Retired allowances: checker, stylesheet, home route ───────────────────
# scripts/check-links.js now matches 5.22.0: upstream shipped the unquoted
# href/id and entity-decoding fix in 5.14.0 (zudolab/zudo-doc#3720).
# scripts/check-links.test.mjs remains the host regression guard and passes
# unchanged against the adopted checker. Its old allowance is unnecessary.
#
# src/styles/global.css now matches 5.22.0. Contrary to the old justification,
# the Noto Sans JP / Futura tokens and header-logo rule were already removed
# by bac307b9fa9c35583a225257ca8b257ce1b71c99 (the v4 default re-scaffold).
# zfb.config.ts explicitly records that custom webfonts were dropped. Keep
# that default-theme decision; do not restore retired fonts. The new template
# page-loading.css import is inactive here: dynamicPageTransition defaults
# to false, so no overlay, spinner, or pending-link bootstrap is rendered.
#
# pages/index.tsx remains the stock package-route re-export. home.wide in
# zfb.config.ts supplies the wide layout without a custom host route.

# ── tsconfig.json: preserve the host type-checking contract ────────────────
# The 5.22.0 template extends "@takazudo/zudo-doc/tsconfig.base.json" and uses
# include: ["src", "pages", "zfb.config.ts"]. Its base explicitly loads the
# package's zfb-config-shim.d.ts and virtual-modules.d.ts and uses react-jsx.
#
# The host deliberately inlines compilerOptions, uses jsx: "preserve", and
# has exclude with NO include. TypeScript 5.9.3 config resolution confirms
# that this includes the root zfb-shim.d.ts; the template excludes that shim
# and loads the package shim instead. The host ambient "zfb/config" module
# is the documented, hand-synced contract checked by `pnpm check`.
# Adopting the template would silently replace that contract and change the
# checked file set (including pages / worktrees exclusions). Preserve the
# complete host config; compiler-option and unused-alias cleanup is separate.
tsconfig.json

# ── scripts/setup-doc-skill.sh: repo-specific skill wiring ─────────────────
# The 5.22.0 template is now suffix-aware: its default would be
# `zudo-css-wisdom`, NOT the old doubled `zudo-css-wisdom-wisdom`. That still
# differs from this repo's required `css-wisdom` name, referenced by
# scripts/generate-css-wisdom.js, .gitignore, and the global skill links.
# Keep the hard pin and rejection of name overrides, and the generator
# pre-step that supplies this repo's curated CSS topic index. The template
# instead writes a generic SKILL.md and, by default, also exports tracked
# project skills. Replacing the host script would change both the skill
# identity and its generated content / linking scope for Claude and Codex.
# Adopted 5.22.0's ensure_symlink conflict handling: replace symlinks, but
# reject existing real files/directories without deleting user-owned content.
scripts/setup-doc-skill.sh

# ── Host brand favicons ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All four host assets retain the orange (#ff9900) "C" mark. The 5.22.0
# template ships its placeholder favicon set (including the purple "Z" SVG),
# so adopting it would replace this site's branding. Keep the host SVG too:
# the package emits its SVG favicon link ahead of the ICO and PNG links.
#
# public/favicon.ico contains SVG markup under an .ico name (`file` reports
# SVG). That predates this reconciliation; correcting its format is separate.
public/favicon.ico
public/favicon-16x16.png
public/favicon-32x32.png
public/favicon.svg
